<section class="bg-hero"><div class="bg-hero-t"><p class="bg-k">An independent handbag guide</p><h1>The bag you choose<br><em>should outlast the season.</em></h1><p class="bg-lead">Bagello helps you choose a handbag with confidence: the right leather for your life, the silhouette that suits how you carry, and the size that actually fits your things.</p><p class="bg-acts"><a class="btn" href="#tools">Find my bag</a><a class="bg-ln" href="leather-types-guide.html">The leather guide</a></p></div><div class="bg-hero-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1793392131101-a717b969ddee?auto=format&fit=crop&w=760&h=860&q=75" alt="person in a houndstooth coat holding a dark leather bag" width="760" height="860" fetchpriority="high"></div></section>

<section class="bg-s"><div class="bg-w"><div class="bg-hh"><p class="bg-k">Six silhouettes</p><h2>Know the shapes</h2></div><div class="bg-shapes">
<article><svg viewBox="0 0 80 60" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 18v-6a14 14 0 0 1 28 0v6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M10 18h60l-6 38H16z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg><h3>Tote</h3><p>Open or zipped, two handles, room for a laptop and a day&rsquo;s things.</p></article>
<article><svg viewBox="0 0 80 60" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M30 20q10-14 20 0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="14" y="20" width="52" height="34" rx="4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M14 30h52" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg><h3>Top-handle</h3><p>Structured and polished, often with a detachable strap.</p></article>
<article><svg viewBox="0 0 80 60" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 4l30 30" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="34" y="28" width="36" height="26" rx="3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M34 36h36" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg><h3>Crossbody</h3><p>Small to medium, hands-free, sits at the hip.</p></article>
<article><svg viewBox="0 0 80 60" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 14q20-14 40 0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M14 16q26 6 52 0l-4 38H18z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg><h3>Hobo</h3><p>Soft and slouchy, crescent-shaped, worn on the shoulder.</p></article>
<article><svg viewBox="0 0 80 60" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M30 14v-4h20v4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M10 14h60v40H10z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M10 14l30 14 30-14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg><h3>Satchel</h3><p>Flat base, flap front, a classic for work and study.</p></article>
<article><svg viewBox="0 0 80 60" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="10" y="20" width="60" height="26" rx="3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M10 20l30 14 30-14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg><h3>Clutch</h3><p>Handheld, no strap, made for evenings and occasions.</p></article></div></div></section>

<section class="bg-tl" id="tools"><div class="bg-w"><div class="bg-hh bg-hh-d"><p class="bg-k">Handbag tools</p><h2>Three questions before you choose</h2></div><div class="bg-vt">
<div class="bg-vt-l" role="tablist" aria-label="Handbag tools" aria-orientation="vertical"><button role="tab" id="bt-1" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="bp-1"><span>I</span>Leather Matcher</button><button role="tab" id="bt-2" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="bp-2"><span>II</span>Silhouette Finder</button><button role="tab" id="bt-3" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="bp-3"><span>III</span>Bag Size Planner</button></div>
<div class="bg-vt-r">
<div class="bg-pn" role="tabpanel" id="bp-1" aria-labelledby="bt-1"><div class="bg-pg"><div><h3>Leather Matcher</h3><p class="bg-pd">Tell us how the bag will live.</p><label for="lm-u">How often you&rsquo;ll carry it<select id="lm-u"><option value="daily">Every day</option><option value="weekly" selected>A few times a week</option><option value="occ">Occasions only</option></select></label><label for="lm-c">Climate<select id="lm-c"><option value="dry">Mostly dry</option><option value="wet">Often rainy</option></select></label><label for="lm-l">Look you prefer<select id="lm-l"><option value="soft">Soft and relaxed</option><option value="struct" selected>Crisp and structured</option><option value="shine">Glossy or statement</option></select></label></div><div class="bg-out" id="lm-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div></div>
<div class="bg-pn" role="tabpanel" id="bp-2" aria-labelledby="bt-2" hidden><div class="bg-pg"><div><h3>Silhouette Finder</h3><p class="bg-pd">Where it goes and how you like to carry.</p><label for="sf-o">Main use<select id="sf-o"><option value="work">Work</option><option value="weekend">Weekends</option><option value="travel">Travel</option><option value="evening">Evenings</option></select></label><label for="sf-c">Carry style<select id="sf-c"><option value="hand">In the hand or crook of the arm</option><option value="shoulder" selected>On the shoulder</option><option value="cross">Crossbody, hands-free</option></select></label></div><div class="bg-out" id="sf-out" aria-live="polite"></div></div></div>
<div class="bg-pn" role="tabpanel" id="bp-3" aria-labelledby="bt-3" hidden><div class="bg-pg"><div><h3>Bag Size Planner</h3><p class="bg-pd">Tick what goes in it every day.</p><div class="bg-ck" id="bs-c"><label><input type="checkbox" value="1" checked> Phone</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="1" checked> Wallet</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="0.5" checked> Keys</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="1"> Sunglasses</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="1.5"> Water bottle</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="2"> Tablet or book</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="6"> Laptop</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="2"> Umbrella</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="1"> Make-up pouch</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="3"> Spare layer</label></div></div><div class="bg-out" id="bs-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div></div>
</div></div></div></section>

<section class="bg-s"><div class="bg-w bg-craft"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1793502618531-38f8ac2d9652?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=680&q=75" alt="cutting a piece of brown leather with a small knife" width="560" height="680" loading="lazy"></figure><div><p class="bg-k">Before you buy</p><h2>Six marks of a well-made bag</h2><ol class="bg-marks"><li><b>Even stitching</b><span>Small, straight and consistent, especially at the handles.</span></li><li><b>Smooth edges</b><span>Painted or folded edges with no fraying or cracking.</span></li><li><b>Solid hardware</b><span>Clasps and zips feel heavy and move smoothly.</span></li><li><b>Reinforced stress points</b><span>Extra stitching or rivets where handles meet the body.</span></li><li><b>A neat lining</b><span>Fitted, without puckering, and stitched securely.</span></li><li><b>A good smell</b><span>Real leather smells rich, never of chemicals.</span></li></ol></div></div></section>

<section class="bg-band"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794752576257-83b13d072625?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1400&h=520&q=75" alt="person in a dark coat holding a bright red bag" width="1400" height="520" loading="lazy"><div class="bg-band-t"><p>&ldquo;A great bag is chosen for the life you have, not the one in the advert.&rdquo;</p></div></section>

<section class="bg-s"><div class="bg-w"><div class="bg-hh"><p class="bg-k">Read further</p><h2>The guides</h2></div><div class="bg-gds"><a href="leather-types-guide.html"><div class="bg-gi"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1793478365902-1246a5a84fdb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=420&q=75" alt="man in a black coat holding a red handbag" width="640" height="420" loading="lazy"></div><div class="bg-gt"><p class="bg-k">Guide I</p><h3>The Leather Types Guide</h3><p>Full-grain, top-grain, pebbled, saffiano-style, suede and patent compared, with care for each.</p></div></a><a href="bag-silhouettes-guide.html"><div class="bg-gi"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792763001513-557316cc0b56?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=420&q=75" alt="black handbag and tote bags" width="640" height="420" loading="lazy"></div><div class="bg-gt"><p class="bg-k">Guide II</p><h3>The Bag Silhouettes Guide</h3><p>Every major shape explained, and how to choose one for your height, routine and wardrobe.</p></div></a></div></div></section>

<section class="bg-s bg-ivory"><div class="bg-w bg-fq"><div><p class="bg-k">FAQ</p><h2>Handbag questions</h2><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1793496638073-0671a341951e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=460&h=340&q=75" alt="crocheted handbags with wooden handles" width="460" height="340" loading="lazy"></div><div class="bg-faq"><details open><summary>What is the most durable handbag leather?</summary><p>Full-grain leathers with a pebbled or grained finish, such as pebbled calf, resist scratches and everyday wear best. They also hide small marks well and develop a pleasant character with age.</p></details><details><summary>What is the difference between full-grain and top-grain leather?</summary><p>Full-grain keeps the whole outer surface of the hide, so it is the strongest and ages best. Top-grain has the surface lightly sanded and finished, which makes it more uniform but slightly less robust.</p></details><details><summary>Which bag shape is most versatile?</summary><p>A medium structured tote or a top-handle bag with a detachable shoulder strap works for office, travel and weekends. Neutral colours such as black, tan or taupe widen the options further.</p></details><details><summary>How should I store a leather handbag?</summary><p>Stuff it lightly with acid-free tissue, keep it in a breathable dust bag, store it upright on a shelf and keep it away from direct sunlight and heat sources.</p></details><details><summary>Is patent leather hard to care for?</summary><p>Patent is easy to wipe clean but can pick up colour from other materials and may crease. Store it separately and avoid leaving it in hot cars.</p></details><details><summary>How heavy should an everyday bag be?</summary><p>Lighter is kinder to shoulders. Many people find an empty bag under about 1 kg comfortable for daily use; wide straps spread the load better than thin ones.</p></details></div></div></section>

<section class="bg-nl"><div class="bg-w bg-nl-g"><h2>The Bagello Letter</h2><p>One handbag explainer each month: a leather, a shape or a care tip.</p><a class="btn" href="mailto:hello@bagello.com?subject=The%20Bagello%20Letter&amp;body=Please%20subscribe%20me.">Subscribe by email</a></div></section>

